# Line endings are part of this repository's output contract. `akr build` emits
# byte-reproducible views and the fixture corpus is compared byte for byte, so a file
# whose endings depend on who checked it out is a source of phantom diffs and false
# fixture failures. One file (crates/akr-cli/tests/commands.rs) was committed with CRLF
# and no rule pinned the convention: `cargo fmt` rewrote it to LF, git reported all ~400
# lines as delete-and-re-add around every small change, and `cargo fmt --check` did not
# flag it, so nothing warned. Pin it here rather than rely on each clone's core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Build outputs that happen to be committed. Never diffed, never normalised.
*.exe binary
